# --- Induction Crucible (T3) ---
tile.unboundtech.induction_crucible.name=Induction Crucible
tc.research_name.INDUCTION_CRUCIBLE=Induction Crucible
tc.research_text.INDUCTION_CRUCIBLE=A crucible that holds no grudge
unboundtech.research_page.INDUCTION_CRUCIBLE.1=Fire argues with water, and in that argument everything in the pot falls apart: iron forgets it was a sword. Every hundred heartbeats the old crucible chews up a grain of what it holds, and devours primal essences outright — sometimes belching flux. It is not a store; it is a slow grinder.<BR><BR>An induction rim does not argue — it heats the water itself, evenly and silently. In such water meanings keep as long as you like, and nothing boils out into the world.
unboundtech.research_page.INDUCTION_CRUCIBLE.2=Four punishments of the old crucible lifted — for twenty units of engineering power per heartbeat.<BR><BR>First: no fire beneath; the rim heats itself, a hundred heartbeats from cold to boil.<BR><BR>Second: nothing decays in storage. What you put in stays put, compound meanings included — which is why the Splitter drinks from it so gladly.<BR><BR>Third: an overfull basin does not spit flux — it politely bounces offerings back.<BR><BR>Fourth: leftovers can be DRAINED — into tubes, jars, to golems, always in alphabetical order of meanings.
unboundtech.research_page.INDUCTION_CRUCIBLE.3=Notes on handling.<BR><BR>It brews everything the old crucible brews, by the same recipes: the basin is the same, only the frame differs. A craft costs fifty measures of water from a thousand-measure tank; a bucket pressed to the frame tops it up or takes it back.<BR><BR>An empty phial carries away eight measures of the first meaning, alphabetically, that has enough to spare.<BR><BR>A redstone vein silences the rim and the basin cools — the contents stay intact. A wrench takes the frame apart with everything inside; a pickaxe spills it on the floor, though at least without flux.

# --- Essentia Bus and Vault (T3) ---
tile.unboundtech.bus_node.name=Bus Node
tile.unboundtech.essentia_conduit_i.name=Essentia Conduit I
tile.unboundtech.essentia_conduit_ii.name=Essentia Conduit II
tile.unboundtech.essentia_conduit_iii.name=Essentia Conduit III
tile.unboundtech.essentia_vault_casing.name=Vault Casing
tile.unboundtech.essentia_vault_controller.name=Vault Controller
tile.unboundtech.essentia_vault_golem_port.name=Vault Golem Port
tc.research_name.ESSENTIA_BUS=Essentia Bus
tc.research_text.ESSENTIA_BUS=A crossroads taught a timetable
unboundtech.research_page.ESSENTIA_BUS.1=A tube is honest and stupid: it carries what is pulled and says nothing of the rest. One meaning at a time — and an estate of twenty meanings grows over with tubes like ivy.<BR><BR>The node is a crossroads taught a timetable. It keeps a sip of every meaning and sends them down a single thread without letting them tangle — and charges its due in current: twenty units of power per sip delivered.
unboundtech.research_page.ESSENTIA_BUS.2=The thread between nodes is the conduit: a glass vein in a tempered thaumium braid where meanings walk single file, each on its own facet. Mechanists call it fibre optics; thaumaturges call it discipline.<BR><BR>The cleaner the glass, the more lanes: a plain vein carries two, one with a vis crystal four, one braided in carbon fibre eight. The lane count shows right on the end face.<BR><BR>The conduit itself charges nothing — the sending node pays.
unboundtech.research_page.ESSENTIA_BUS.3=Notes on handling.<BR><BR>The node reads suction like a tube: a thirsty neighbour gets, a full one gives. There are no separate inlets and outlets.<BR><BR>Five faces take tubes, the sixth takes the thread; every tube gets its own lane with an eight-sip buffer. More tubes than lanes — the extras wait, and the node complains honestly when asked with an empty hand.<BR><BR>Service is always alphabetical by meaning — no luck involved.
tc.research_name.ESSENTIA_VAULT=Essentia Vault
tc.research_text.ESSENTIA_VAULT=A library sorted into shelves
unboundtech.research_page.ESSENTIA_VAULT.1=Twenty-seven plates, and inside — a silence sorted into shelves. Every meaning lies apart, labelled, arguing with no neighbour.<BR><BR>Golems run here as to a library: take, carry, return. The library, however, goes dark the moment the wire is pulled — and then nobody takes anything.
unboundtech.research_page.ESSENTIA_VAULT.2=Stack a cube three by three by three: twenty-five blind casings, a controller in the middle of one face looking outward, and exactly one golem alcove on any side.<BR><BR>It holds three hundred eighty-four sips, but no more than ninety-six of one meaning: a store of many-a-little, not a bucket for one. The old Reservoir is still better when you need two hundred fifty-six measures of the same thing — and it asks for no current, either.
unboundtech.research_page.ESSENTIA_VAULT.3=Notes on handling.<BR><BR>Every occupied shelf costs one unit of power per heartbeat; every sip in or out costs twenty. Current gone — the library goes dark entirely: nothing in, nothing out.<BR><BR>One meaning clogged — the rest flow on; everything clogged — the controller glows red.<BR><BR>An empty phial at the controller carries away eight sips of the first meaning alphabetically. A wrench lifts the controller with all its contents; a pickaxe loses them.

# --- Flux Revolver and ammunition (T3) ---
item.unboundtech.casing.name=Casing
item.unboundtech.cartridge_incendiary.name=Incendiary Cartridge
