tile.unboundtech.photon_light.name=Light
unboundtech.tooltip.casing=Empty. Decides exactly when the flash happens
unboundtech.tooltip.cartridge_incendiary=Alumentum in a casing: sets the target alight for five seconds
unboundtech.tooltip.cartridge_illuminating=Nitor in a casing: a minute of light at the point of impact, half damage
unboundtech.tooltip.revolver_empty=Drum empty — Sneak-use to reload
unboundtech.tooltip.revolver_damage=Base damage
tc.research_name.FLUX_REVOLVER=Flux Revolver
tc.research_text.FLUX_REVOLVER=Not powerful. Predictable
unboundtech.research_page.FLUX_REVOLVER.1=The first thing an apprentice does upon earning the right to handle alumentum is put it in a tube and see what happens. The second is learning from a master how to do that and keep the hand.<BR><BR>The revolver stands exactly between the first and the second: it is not powerful, it is PREDICTABLE — and for a first barrel that matters more.<BR><BR>The first mechanists loaded barrels with raw alumentum, and the first mechanists did not live long. The casing is not about convenience: it decides exactly when the flash happens.
unboundtech.research_page.FLUX_REVOLVER.2=The drum holds six charges of one kind — it refuses to mix. Changing kinds means emptying the drum entirely; seating each charge takes time, and a dozen-odd heartbeats for a full drum are felt.<BR><BR>The projectile flies, and it can be seen: alchemy, not lightning. Half the casings fall at your feet — bend down and gather them, a tempered ingot yields only eight.
unboundtech.research_page.FLUX_REVOLVER.3=Two kinds of charge for now.<BR><BR>Incendiary — alumentum in a casing: full force, and five seconds of fire.<BR><BR>Illuminating — nitor in a casing: half force, but it leaves a minute of light where it lands. Shoot into the dark — and the dark ends.<BR><BR>The grip will do for a knock — but that is courtesy, not fencing.

# --- Schema Rings (T3) ---
item.unboundtech.ring_frame.name=Ring of Frame
item.unboundtech.ring_drive.name=Ring of Drive
item.unboundtech.ring_stride.name=Ring of Stride
item.unboundtech.ring_brace.name=Ring of Brace
unboundtech.tooltip.ring_frame=Reminds the body of soundness: two hearts and toughness against piercing
unboundtech.tooltip.ring_drive=Reminds the hands of speed: a faster, one-heavier strike
unboundtech.tooltip.ring_stride=Reminds the legs of lightness: an eighth over each step
unboundtech.tooltip.ring_brace=Reminds the feet of roots: half the shoves miss, two measures of armour
unboundtech.tooltip.ring_upkeep=Eats two units of power per heartbeat; drained — silent, but whole
tc.research_name.SCHEMA_RINGS=Schema Rings
tc.research_text.SCHEMA_RINGS=The body agrees — while there is something to remind it with
unboundtech.research_page.SCHEMA_RINGS.1=A ring does not conjure. A ring REMINDS the body of what it could have been, had it been built to a blueprint rather than as it happened. The body, strangely, agrees — while the ring has something to remind it with.<BR><BR>Four blueprints: Frame holds life, Drive holds the strike, Stride holds the step, Brace holds the line. The stone in the setting tells you which one you hold.
unboundtech.research_page.SCHEMA_RINGS.2=The price is two units of engineering power per heartbeat from each ring. A pair eats more than the Aetheric Generator gives at a steady pace: your own converter will not feed them — you need a grid or a reserve. Any low-tier charger fills a ring.<BR><BR>Drained — the body forgets the reminder at once, but the ring is whole: power returns, and so does the memory.
unboundtech.research_page.SCHEMA_RINGS.3=Notes on handling.<BR><BR>Two identical rings do not argue with the body twice: the second stays silent.<BR><BR>These rings grant no runic shield at all — that is their price. The old runic rings give a shield; these give the body itself. Two slots — choose.<BR><BR>Taking off the Ring of Frame, the body honestly returns the extra hearts — but never what you live by.

# --- Focus of Charge (T3) ---
item.unboundtech.focus_charge.name=Focus of Charge
tc.research_name.FOCUS_CHARGE=Focus of Charge
tc.research_text.FOCUS_CHARGE=A portable socket of dubious provenance
unboundtech.research_page.FOCUS_CHARGE.1=The first thaumaturge to point a wand at a machine expected it to get angry. The machine ate its fill.<BR><BR>Ever since, shop ledgers list the wand as "a portable socket of dubious provenance", and the Guild's ledgers list it as "a disgrace".
unboundtech.research_page.FOCUS_CHARGE.2=The focus pours the wand's vis into engineering power: a thousand units per measure of vis, Order and Fire in equal parts. Twice worse than the Aetheric Generator — the price of fieldwork, not a power plant.<BR><BR>Point it at a machine and the machine feeds; hold a chargeable thing in the other hand and the thing feeds. Whatever takes no charge will say so.<BR><BR>The focus never takes back: a socket, not a pump.

# --- Techno-Spirit and Charged Spark (T3) ---
entity.unboundtech.techno_spirit.name=Techno-Spirit
item.unboundtech.charged_spark.name=Charged Spark
unboundtech.tooltip.charged_spark=Keeps while carried; dropped, it slowly fades
tc.research_name.TECHNO_SPIRITS=Techno-Spirits
tc.research_text.TECHNO_SPIRITS=Mechanists insist it is not yet life
unboundtech.research_page.TECHNO_SPIRITS.1=Where current runs for years past a node, the air begins to imitate. First it is just a spark out of rhythm, then a spark that hangs in the air longer than it should — and then it is looking at you.<BR><BR>Mechanists insist it is not yet life. Thaumaturges say nothing — they have seen such things before.
unboundtech.research_page.TECHNO_SPIRITS.2=The spirit is not wicked — it is hungry. It drifts to a working machine and feeds on its rhythm; strike it and it snaps back with a discharge and flees.<BR><BR>But do not suffer them out of politeness: an unpunished spirit calls a second, the second a third, up to five in a yard. A walk through the shop every few minutes with anything in hand is enough — a chased spirit forgets to call its kin.<BR><BR>The owner of a full nano-thaumic suit will know no peace: to a spirit he is himself a great walking machine by a node.
unboundtech.research_page.TECHNO_SPIRITS.3=A slain spirit always sheds a Charged Spark — a clot of current locked in a film of vis. No hand holds more than eight, and dropped on the ground one melts away in minutes.<BR><BR>There is nowhere to spend Sparks yet. But Guild records mention gates that open to nothing else — do not throw them away.

# --- Technomancer Villager (T3) ---
entity.Villager.technomancer=Technomancer
tc.research_name.TECHNOMANCER=Exile of Two Schools
tc.research_text.TECHNOMANCER=Curses both sides equally
unboundtech.research_page.TECHNOMANCER.1=The tower threw him out for measuring vis with an ammeter. The workshop — because a machine spoke in his presence. Now he lives on the outskirts, in a shed under a tin roof, mending for both schools what they broke in each other. He takes emeralds and curses both sides equally.
unboundtech.research_page.TECHNOMANCER.2=Thaumaturges reject science: the measurable denies revelation, and calculation cheapens years given to the knowing of meanings. Mechanists pay in kind: what cannot be taken apart does not, for them, exist.<BR><BR>The technomancer is the one who refused to choose, and so is needed by neither. Had the schools spoken to each other, the bridge between them would have been built without you.<BR><BR>He gladly buys up Charged Sparks — he of all people knows their worth. He will sell them to no one, at any price.

# --- Flux Arquebus and T4 cartridges ---
item.unboundtech.flux_arquebus.name=Flux Arquebus
item.unboundtech.cartridge_vis.name=Vis Cartridge
item.unboundtech.cartridge_flux.name=Flux Cartridge
unboundtech.tooltip.cartridge_vis=A phial of vis in a casing: half the blow passes any armour
unboundtech.tooltip.cartridge_flux=A Flux Charge in a casing: a cloud of murk at the point of impact, friend or foe
unboundtech.tooltip.arquebus_loaded=Chambered
unboundtech.tooltip.arquebus_empty=Barrel empty — Sneak-use with a cartridge in inventory
tc.research_name.FLUX_ARQUEBUS=Flux Arquebus
tc.research_text.FLUX_ARQUEBUS=One shot that decides
unboundtech.research_page.FLUX_ARQUEBUS.1=The revolver forgives: six tries, and one will land. The arquebus does not forgive and does not ask forgiveness. One charge, a long faceted barrel, and forty heartbeats to seat the next — shoot as if the shot were your last, because it is.<BR><BR>In return it strikes twice as far, four times as true, and through: the first taker gets the full blow, the second behind him — half. No mechanist barrel can do that.
unboundtech.research_page.FLUX_ARQUEBUS.2=It cannot be assembled on a bench: this is a work, not a trinket. The infusion altar takes your revolver whole — polite predictability and all — and draws it out into a cubit and a half of faceted barrel on a greatwood stock.<BR><BR>The recoil shoves in earnest: mind the cliff edge. Casings still fall at your feet — bend down.
unboundtech.research_page.FLUX_ARQUEBUS.3=Two new charges for the long barrel.<BR><BR>The vis cartridge — a full phial in a casing: half the blow passes any armour, as vis itself does.<BR><BR>The flux cartridge — thickened murk: a cloud of flux gas rises at the point of impact, and it does not care who stands in it. Do not shoot at your own feet. Seriously.

